          "question": "Asexual reproduction takes place through budding in:<br/>(a) Amoeba<br/>(b) Yeast<br/>(c) Plasmodium<br/>(d) Leishmania",
          "solution": [
            "<b>Correct Answer: (b) Yeast</b>",
            "<br/><b>Detailed Explanation:</b>",
            "1. <b>Budding</b> is an asexual mode of reproduction where a small bulb-like projection, called a <b>bud</b>, emerges from the parent cell.",
            "2. In <b>Yeast (a unicellular fungus)</b>, the nucleus undergoes mitosis, and one daughter nucleus migrates into the developing bud.",
            "3. As the bud grows, it may form a chain of buds before finally constricting at its base and detaching to become an independent, viable individual.",
            "4. <i>Other options:</i> Amoeba reproduces by binary fission, Plasmodium by multiple fission within a cyst, and Leishmania by longitudinal binary fission."
          ],
          "answer": "(b) Yeast (Yeast reproduces asexually by developing small buds that grow and detach from the parent cell).",
