          "answer": "Unicellular organisms reproduce simply via asexual cell division (binary/multiple fission, budding) where the whole cell divides. Multicellular organisms possess specialized cells and dedicated reproductive organs (gonads, flowers) that produce haploid gametes through meiosis and undergo sexual fertilization."
